"""Complete the remaining short solutions and restore the verified 2008 Q2 figure."""
from pathlib import Path
import json
solutions=[
('amc-up-2008',2,'DATA-03','Between 1 and 2 the number line has ten equal intervals, so each short interval is one tenth, or 0.1. The arrow points three intervals after 1. Its value is 1 + 3×0.1 = 1.3. Read the scale before counting the small ticks.'),
('amc-up-2008',4,'FRAC-04','Half full means one of two equal parts of the 7500-litre capacity. Divide by 2: 7500 ÷ 2 = 3750 litres. Check by doubling: 3750 + 3750 = 7500.'),
('amc-up-2008',5,'RATE-01','One bottle fills three glasses of the stated size. Seven identical bottles therefore fill seven groups of three glasses: 7 × 3 = 21. The question asks for glasses, so multiply by the number of glasses per bottle.'),
('amc-up-2008',6,'DIG-01','An increase is the new price minus the old price: 153.5 − 149.9. From 149.9 to 150 is 0.1, then from 150 to 153.5 is 3.5. Add 0.1 + 3.5 = 3.6 cents per litre. Keep the answer in cents, not dollars.'),
('amc-up-2008',9,'ALG-01','Three equal boxes and two loose cars contain 17 cars altogether. Remove the two loose cars: 17 − 2 = 15 cars are in the boxes. Divide equally among three boxes: 15 ÷ 3 = 5 cars per box. Check: 3 × 5 + 2 = 17.'),
('amc-up-2023',3,'ALG-01','The two visible dice show 5 and 3, for a total of 8. The three dice must total 12, so the missing die shows 12 − 8 = 4. Check: 5 + 3 + 4 = 12.'),
('amc-up-2024',1,'RATE-01','Each birthday increases the age by one. Fourteen years after the birth year 2016 is 2016 + 14 = 2030. Thus the fourteenth birthday is in 2030.')]
solutions += [
('amc-up-2007',13,'LOGIC-02','Use rows, columns and the four 2×2 blocks together. In the bottom-left block, the missing numbers are 2 and 3; the third row already has 3, so its first entry is 2 and the bottom row has 3 in column 2. The third row then ends in 4. Column 2 now forces 4 in row 2. Continuing with the same missing-number rule gives rows 1,2,4,3 / 3,4,2,1 / 2,1,3,4 / 4,3,1,2. The four corners are 1, 3, 4 and 2, so their sum is 10.'),
('amc-up-2007',16,'GEO-02','Across the 12-metre width, the left and right paths use 4 and 2 metres. The lawn width is therefore 12 − 4 − 2 = 6 metres. Along the 8-metre height, the top and bottom paths use 3 and 1 metres, leaving 8 − 3 − 1 = 4 metres. Multiply the two lawn dimensions: 6 × 4 = 24 square metres. Subtract widths on the matching direction before finding the area.'),
('amc-up-2007',25,'LOGIC-02','Write ages as A,B,C,D,E,F,G. Since D = 3B and all ages are 1 to 7, B is 1 or 2. Also F > A > G, so F,A,G must be in decreasing order. If B = 2 and D = 6, C = E + 4 allows (C,E) = (5,1) or (7,3). These leave (F,A,G) = (7,4,3) or (5,4,1); in each case A + G equals F, contradicting A + G > F. Thus B = 1 and D = 3. Now the only available pair four years apart is (C,E) = (6,2). The remaining ages are 4,5,7, forcing F = 7, A = 5, G = 4. Check 5 + 4 > 7. Ace is 5.'),
('amc-up-2007',26,'SPATIAL-04','There are two forward roads P→Q, two forward roads Q→R, one reverse road Q→P, one reverse road R→Q, and two final roads R→S. Split by which reverse roads are used. Neither: 2×2×2 = 8 routes. Only Q→P: the two P→Q roads must both be used, in either order, then choose Q→R and R→S: 2×2×2 = 8. Only R→Q similarly gives 8. Both reverse roads: the town sequence is either P-Q-P-Q-R-Q-R-S or P-Q-R-Q-P-Q-R-S. For each sequence choose the order of the two P→Q roads, the order of the two Q→R roads and the final road: 2×2×2 = 8. Thus the total is 8 + 8 + 8 + 2×8 = 40. The cases cannot overlap.'),
('amc-up-2007',28,'SPATIAL-03','Imagine a vertical cut halfway across the 4-unit width. Each half is a 3×2 rectangle containing 6 squares, so an even number of dominoes must cross the cut: either 0 or 2. With none crossing, each 3×2 half has three tilings (three horizontal dominoes, or a horizontal domino above or below a pair of vertical dominoes). The two halves can be chosen independently, giving 3×3 = 9. With two crossing, they must cross in the top two rows or the bottom two rows. Each choice forces the remaining tiles, giving 2 more. Crossing only the top and bottom rows leaves isolated corner squares and cannot work. Total: 9 + 2 = 11.')]
rows=[dict(exam_id=e,question_number=n,category=k,explanation=s) for e,n,k,s in solutions]
body='<path d="M30 90H421" stroke="black"/>'
for i in range(34):
 x=30+i*11.7;body+=f'<path d="M{x} 90v{16 if i%10==0 else 12 if i%5==0 else 6}" stroke="black"/>'
 if i%10==0:body+=f'<text x="{x}" y="132" text-anchor="middle" font-size="17">{i//10}</text>'
x=30+13*11.7;body+=f'<path d="M{x} 48V90m-9 -10l9 10l9 -10" stroke="black" fill="none"/>'
rows[0]['figure_svg']=f'<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 450 160" role="img" aria-label="Number line labelled 0, 1, 2, 3 with ten intervals per unit; arrow three intervals after 1"><rect width="450" height="160" fill="white"/>{body}</svg>'
next(r for r in rows if r['exam_id']=='amc-up-2007' and r['question_number']==25)['stem']='Ace, Bea, Cec, Dee, Eve, Fie and Geo are 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 and 7 years old in some order. Dee is three times as old as Bea. Cec is four years older than Eve. Fie is older than Ace and Ace is older than Geo. The combined ages of Ace and Geo are greater than the age of Fie. How old is Ace?'
Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3].joinpath('rebuild/archive-finishing.json').write_text(json.dumps(rows))
